"{\"url\":\"https://registry.isometric.com/project/prj_1KA95092G1S093EM\",\"title\":\"Reforesting the Brazilian Amazon Project 1 — Isometric\",\"head\":[\"VALIDATED\",\"BIOSPHERE\",\"100Y+\",\"Reforesting the Brazilian Amazon Project 1\",\"Mombak\",\"ISSUED\",\"21,771.53\",\"BUFFER POOL\",\"2,286.012\",\"CREDITING PERIOD\",\"31 Mar 2023 to 30 Mar 2073\",\"Summary\"],\"issued_header\":\"21,771.53\",\"buffer_header\":\"2,286.012\",\"crediting\":\"31 Mar 2023 to 30 Mar 2073\",\"verifier\":\"350Solutions\",\"code\":\"84R7\",\"approval\":\"01 Jul 2026\",\"protocol_current\":\"Reforestation v1.1\",\"protocol_baseline\":null,\"cert_issued\":\"21,771.53\",\"cert_retired\":\"0\",\"cert_buffer\":\"2,286.012\",\"reversal\":null,\"showing\":[\"Showing 4 of 4\",\"Showing 3 of 3\"],\"tables\":[{\"heads\":[\"Submission date\",\"Title\",\"Download\"],\"rows\":[[\"01 Jul 2026\",\"GHG Statement Report\",\"PDF | ->\"],[\"01 Jul 2026\",\"PDD\",\"PDF | ->\"],[\"01 Jul 2026\",\"Validation and Verification Report\",\"PDF | ->\"],[\"02 May 2026\",\"Public Comment Period Summary\",\"PDF | ->\"]]},{\"heads\":[\"Issue date\",\"Issued\",\"Buffer pool\",\"Supplier allocation\"],\"rows\":[[\"01 Jul 2026\",\"10,128.03\",\"1,063.444\",\"9,064.586\"],[\"01 Jul 2026\",\"8,555.6\",\"898.338\",\"7,657.262\"],[\"01 Jul 2026\",\"3,087.9\",\"324.23\",\"2,763.67\"]]}],\"links\":[{\"h\":\"/supplier/spl_1JWY4JWJK1S05RE6\",\"t\":\"Mombak\"},{\"h\":\"https://350solutions.com\",\"t\":\"350Solutions\"},{\"h\":\"/protocol/reforestation/1.1\",\"t\":\"Reforestation v1.1\"},{\"h\":\"?view=map&area=fpa_1KK9FHQCW1S0D0HT\",\"t\":\"Turmalina\"},{\"h\":\"https://maplibre.org\",\"t\":\"MapLibre\"},{\"h\":\"https://carto.com/about-carto/\",\"t\":\"CARTO\"},{\"h\":\"https://www.openstreetmap.org/about/\",\"t\":\"OpenStreetMap\"},{\"h\":\"https://storage.googleapis.com/isometric--production--eu--public-documents/spl_1JWY4JWJK1S05RE6/prj_1KA95092G1S093EM/pjd_1KWERG85D1S0RJ4Y/pdd.pdf\",\"t\":\"Project Design Document | 01 Jul 2026\"},{\"h\":\"/ghg-entry/rmv_1KKAC5BT01S0QSRX?tab=calculation-view\",\"t\":\"See GHG entry →\"},{\"h\":\"https://storage.googleapis.com/isometric--production--eu--public-documents/spl_1JWY4JWJK1S05RE6/prj_1KA95092G1S093EM/pjd_1KWERJ1M61S0ZVW8/ghg_statement_report.pdf\",\"t\":\"PDF | ->\"},{\"h\":\"https://storage.googleapis.com/isometric--production--eu--public-documents/spl_1JWY4JWJK1S05RE6/prj_1KA95092G1S093EM/pjd_1KWERG85D1S0RJ4Y/pdd.pdf\",\"t\":\"PDF | ->\"},{\"h\":\"https://storage.googleapis.com/isometric--production--eu--public-documents/spl_1JWY4JWJK1S05RE6/prj_1KA95092G1S093EM/pjd_1KWERFKVK1S0H8DM/validation_and_verification_report.pdf\",\"t\":\"PDF | ->\"},{\"h\":\"https://storage.googleapis.com/isometric--production--eu--public-documents/spl_1JWY4JWJK1S05RE6/prj_1KA95092G1S093EM/pjd_1KQVMFHRA1S06J39/public_comment_period_summary.pdf\",\"t\":\"PDF | ->\"},{\"h\":\"/protocol/reforestation/1.2#appendix-e-reforestation-risk-assessment\",\"t\":\"View risk assessment methodology\"}],\"text\":\"VALIDATED\\nBIOSPHERE\\n100Y+\\nReforesting the Brazilian Amazon Project 1\\nMombak\\nISSUED\\n21,771.53\\nBUFFER POOL\\n2,286.012\\nCREDITING PERIOD\\n31 Mar 2023 to 30 Mar 2073\\nSummary\\nProject areas\\nRemoval method\\nCalculation overview\\nProject documentation\\nCertificates\\nReversal risk\\nSummary\\n\\nThis project catalyzes the large-scale reforestation of degraded pasturelands in Brazil, transforming low-productivity cattle ranching areas into resilient, biodiverse carbon sinks. Our approach integrates two primary reforestation strategies: the active planting of diverse native species and Assisted Natural Regeneration (ANR). By selecting species for their survival rates, stress tolerance, and carbon sequestration potential—including several endangered species—we ensure the creation of a high-functioning forest ecosystem. Upon the removal of cattle, the project implements rigorous maintenance protocols, including the establishment of firebreaks and the control of invasive species to ensure natural regeneration flourishes. The project maintains high standards of permanence and additionality by securing land rights through either direct property acquisition or long-term rural partnership agreements with local landowners.\\n\\nPROJECT DETAILS\\nCurrent verifier\\n350Solutions\\n->\\nProject code\\n84R7\\nApproval date\\n01 Jul 2026\\nCurrent protocol version\\nReforestation v1.1\\nAccreditation\\n⌘ + scroll to zoom\\nReforesting the Brazilian Amazon Project 1\\nProject areas\\nView full screen\\nAreas\\nTurmalina\\nLayers\\nSatellite\\nMapLibre | © CARTO, © OpenStreetMap contributors\\nHow carbon is being removed\\n\\nBiosphere carbon dioxide removal (CDR) harnesses the natural capacity of terrestrial and near-coastal ecosystems to absorb and store carbon for extended periods. These pathways utilize the biological processes of forests, soils, wetlands, and other ecosystems to capture carbon dioxide from the atmosphere and sequester it in biomass, soil organic matter, and sediments. Approaches to biosphere CDR include Reforestation, Agroforestry, Improved Forest Management, Mangrove Restoration, Peatland Restoration, and Soil Carbon Enhancement. Biosphere pathways often provide many co-benefits around the protection and enhancement of biodiversity alongside sustainable development for local communities.\\n\\nProject Design Document\\n01 Jul 2026\\nCalculation overview\\nCalculations demonstrating 10,128.03 tCO₂e removed from Reforesting the Brazilian Amazon Project 1 on 23 Oct 2025\\nSee GHG entry →\\nNet CO₂e Removed\\n10,128.030 tCO₂e\\nSequestrations\\n10,242.466 tCO₂e\\n-\\nActivities\\n114.436 tCO₂e\\n⌘ + scroll to zoom\\nView full screen\\nProject documentation\\nSubmission date\\tTitle\\tDownload\\n01 Jul 2026\\tGHG Statement Report\\tPDF\\n->\\n\\n01 Jul 2026\\tPDD\\tPDF\\n->\\n\\n01 Jul 2026\\tValidation and Verification Report\\tPDF\\n->\\n\\n02 May 2026\\tPublic Comment Period Summary\\tPDF\\n->\\nShowing 4 of 4\\nPrevious\\nNext\\nCertificates\\nIssued\\n21,771.53\\nRetired\\n0\\nBuffer pool\\n2,286.012\\nCrediting period\\n31 Mar 2023 to 30 Mar 2073\\nIssuances\\nRetirements\\nIssue date\\tIssued\\tBuffer pool\\tSupplier allocation\\n01 Jul 2026\\t10,128.03\\t1,063.444\\t9,064.586\\n01 Jul 2026\\t8,555.6\\t898.338\\t7,657.262\\n01 Jul 2026\\t3,087.9\\t324.23\\t2,763.67\\nShowing 3 of 3\\nPrevious\\nNext\\nReversal risk\\n\\nThe risk of reversal for this project is calculated for each removal using a standardized risk assessment and falls between 10% and 20%. The average risk of reversal across all removals in this project is 10.5%.\\n\\nTo date, this project has contributed 2,286.012 certificates to the Reforestation Buffer Pool, which holds a total of 2,286.012 certificates.\\n\\nMombak has no reversals to date.\\n\\nView risk assessment methodology\"}"